As quoted from <34022@mimsy.umd.edu> by leonard@mimsy.umd.edu (Leonard Dickens):
+---------------
| 4) Have lawful altars only bless water for lawful (or maybe neutral)
| characters.  
+---------------

Likewise for chaotic altars and unholy water.

---------------
| 7) Have lawful sentient monsters (dwarves, elves) occasionally become
| tamed to lawful characters, and thereby work with the player to kill
| the baddies on the level.  Have this work very infrequently for
+---------------

Again, likewise for chaotics and possibly even for neutrals.

Aside from these, good ideas.  Although I do wish there were a way to reverse
"blessed" vs. "cursed" for chaotics without causing headaches.  Headaches
such as: if your lawful priest kills an orc which leaves behind a cursed
weapon, and is subsequently killed, and a chaotic character happens upon the
bones level, s/he will find a *blessed* weapon; not good.  The only fix I
see for this is to store an absolute blessed/cursed state as well, so the
weapon would be cursed regardless of who picked it up.  The code would be a
nightmare, though.

On the other hand, the result of an unmodified reversal of blessed/cursed
state for chaotics could be seen as a feature.  And then again:  what would
the effect be for neutrals?  Possibly they don't get cursed stuff, just
chaotic or lawful stuff... each with its own benefits and pitfalls.

(Pitfalls with a lawful item?  Consider:

(explorer returns to a level where a formerly tame pet is)
Fido hits!  Wizard is about to die.
Throw what? *
(no food in inventory)
(attack pet)
Your lawful sword refuses!
Fido hits! --more--
You die...

This could make things interesting, too....)

